I understand that most jbopli today are using the Roman alphabet, and
that's fine, but not really cultural neutral. So I don't understand why
{lo'a} is defined as "shift letterals to *Lojban* (Roman) alphabet." I
think every alphabet should be equally lojbanic, or? If lojban would have a
default alphabet I think it should be Tengwar, since that's the most
cultural neutral (and also phonetical) alphabet. Anyway, I'm already using
tengwar sometimes, so I really think it would be nice to have a BY1 for
tengwar also. Maybe {te'i}?
mu'o mi'e jongausib

